  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "In \\(\\triangle ABC\\) and \\(\\triangle DEF\\), \\(\\angle A=\\angle D\\), \\(AB=DE\\), and \\(\\angle B=\\angle E\\). Which criterion establishes congruence?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "AAS",
    "B": "SAS",
    "C": "ASA",
    "D": "SSS"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(AB\\) is the included side between \\(\\angle A\\) and \\(\\angle B\\), and \\(DE\\) is the included side between \\(\\angle D\\) and \\(\\angle E\\). Two angles and their included side are respectively equal, so ASA directly proves \\(\\triangle ABC\\cong\\triangle DEF\\), giving choice C.\n\nThe triangle angle sum also gives\n\\[\n\\angle C=180^\\circ-\\angle A-\\angle B\n=180^\\circ-\\angle D-\\angle E=\\angle F.\n\\]\nUsing the equal angles at \\(A,C\\) and \\(D,F\\), the equal sides \\(AB\\) and \\(DE\\) are opposite \\(\\angle C\\) and \\(\\angle F\\). Therefore AAS also establishes congruence, giving choice A. Both A and C work as written; C is the intended answer only under a direct-given-pattern interpretation.",
